      "content": "Interesting. You mentioned the \"grammatical errors\" in Sample B as the reason for the low score. But if you look closely at the actual logic, the speaker is saying the exact same thing as Sample A—just using different words. Is it really about the content being less competent, or is it just the way they're talking? Like, if someone has these same high-level strategic ideas but just uses a more casual or dialect-heavy way of speaking, are they actually less capable of being a CEO?",
