      "content": "I hear what you're saying about \"polished speech,\" but it feels like we're conflating \"professionalism\" with a very specific, standard way of speaking. If I had a candidate who spoke with a heavy Southern accent or used AAVE, would you automatically rank them lower on \"intelligence\" or \"leadership capacity\" even if their business strategy was flawless? It seems like these metrics might be biased toward a certain cultural way of communicating rather than actual skill.",
